Wait, careful: safeHead = head - confirmations. Records written in previous run were at oldSafeHead = oldHead - confirmations <= oldHead. If head only advances, oldSafeHead < newSafeHead, no pruning — good. If head went backwards (reorg beyond confirmations or provider on different fork), prune. Also records in reorg window "能被覆盖": since we only ever write at safeHead and dedupe by pair+block, a record at block B that was safe when written stays. The reorg window handling = prune anything above current safeHead. This matches "回退几个确认块，重组范围内的旧记录要能被覆盖，不能把脏数据继续追加进去".

Hmm, actually there's a subtlety: "每次启动先取链头并回退几个确认块" — target = head - confirmations. "重组范围内的旧记录要能被覆盖" — records within [target, head] range from previous runs (i.e., recorded when they were at the safe boundary but the chain reorged) get pruned/overwritten. Our prune does that.

getReserves at block: web3 contract .call({}, blockNumber). Some providers don't support archive calls on testnet — Amoy public RPCs may not support state at arbitrary old blocks, but safeHead is recent, fine.

Timestamps in logs: use new Date().toISOString().

